<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Mill demand lifts some bids.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Mill demand lifts some bids.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat firmed at scattered locations in Kansas on continued mill demand, grain merchandisers said Wednesday.</p>
<p>But dealers complained that the continued firmness in basis levels had done little to elicit grain from the country. Movement was extremely slack, they said.</p>
<p>&quot;The premiums have crept up for a very good reason -- we obviously need the wheat for the grind, but I don't think there's a hell of a lot left out there to buy,&quot; a south-central Kansas dealer said.  </p>
